SUMMARY:Live Music Night: Local Frequencies\, The NYC Sound
DESCRIPTION:This evening is all about exploring the music\, art\, and socia
 l histories that have shaped New York City's creative identity from the gr
 ound up. Hosted at Olio Lighthouse in Brooklyn\, we'll gather to discuss h
 ow local artists and community-driven movements have defined the city thro
 ugh sound\, expression\, and cultural innovation.&nbsp\;Part concert and p
 art conversation we'll move back and forth between learning about and then
  exploring the sounds that have shaped NYC.&nbsp\;New York's reputation as
  a global entertainment capital was built not only by internationally reco
 gnized artists\, but also by the countless neighborhood scenes\, independe
 nt venues\, and creative communities that gave rise to new artistic forms.
  From jazz in Harlem and salsa in the Bronx and Spanish Harlem\, to punk o
 n the Lower East Side and hip-hop born in community spaces throughout the 
 boroughs\, the city's cultural history has been shaped by artists respondi
 ng to the realities of their time and place.&nbsp\;Through live performanc
 e\, discussion\, visual art\, listening sessions\, and storytelling\, Nati
 ve Frequencies: The New York Sound\, highlights the cultural attitudes\, s
 ocial conditions\, and creative movements that emerged from New York's nei
 ghborhoods and became defining elements of the city's identity. The evenin
 g centers local artists\, past and present\, whose work reflects the lived
  experiences\, resilience\, and imagination of New Yorkers.&nbsp\;By conne
 cting historical movements with contemporary creators\, Native Frequencies
  creates space for dialogue\, preservation\, and celebration of New York's
  living cultural heritage.&nbsp\;Our musicians for the evening: Alexis Mar
 celo is a New York City–based pianist and improviser whose work moves th
 roughprogressive jazz\, creative music\, and the broader African American 
 musical tradition. Heholds a degree in African American Music/Jazz Piano f
 rom the University of MassachusettsAmherst\, where he had the privilege of
  studying with the legendary multi-instrumentalistYusef Lateef. In recent 
 years\, Marcelo has built a wide-ranging career as a freelancemusician\, p
 erforming with artists including Adam Rudolph\, James Brandon Lewis\, Crai
 gHarris\, Justin Hicks\, and Helga Davis. His debut solo album\, Alexis Ma
 rcelo – Solo Piano\,was released on Intakt Records and is currently bein
 g presented in performance. He canalso be heard on new work with Rudolph
 ’s Sunrise Trio and Hu Vibrational. Upcomingappearances include a Yusef 
 Lateef tribute in Massachusetts and performances with the Sun Ra Arkestra.
 &nbsp\;Evening Flow7:00 PM — Doors open. Settle in\, grab a drink\, and 
 meet a friend.7:30 PM — The evening begins: an opening set with song-by-
 song explorations led by Alexis Marcelo&nbsp\;8:30 PM — Intermission and
  Mingling9:00 PM — Encore!&nbsp\;10:00 PM — Last call at the bar as we
  wind down the evening.This show will be a mix of seated and standing room
 . Come on time if you'd like a chair.&nbsp\;What Is Think Olio?Think Olio 
 is an ongoing experiment in lifelong learning. We are a community of open-
 minded people who gather to exchange ideas with new friends and connect ov
 er art\, literature\, and philosophy.Check out our full calendarOur $30 me
 mbership gives you two events for the price of one!&nbsp\;An Olio is what 
 we call the social learning events we’ve been organizing since 2015. A b
 lend between a lecture and a house party\, Olios are led by a teacher who 
 loves sharing their passions and the room is filled with curious\, open-mi
 nded New Yorkers.&nbsp\;Our goal is to spark new perspectives\, ignite cur
 iosity\, and enjoy ourselves socially\, an alternative to typical nightlif
 e options.Disclaimer: By purchasing a ticket\, you agree to have your phot
 o/video used for social media/marketing materials. If you prefer to not ha
 ve your photo taken\, feel free to send us a note. Photo by Zhi-Da Zhong\n
 \nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/live_music_night_nat
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/live_music_night_nat
END:VEVENT
